315 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Lord Shiva's Significance: Shiva, one of the principal deities in Hinduism, is revered as the supreme being, the source of all creation and destruction. His cosmic dance, embodied in the Nataraja form, signifies the cyclical nature of the universe, the constant interplay of creation and destruction, and the underlying rhythm of life itself. Symbolism of the Dance: The Nataraja statue portrays Shiva dancing within a ring of fire, representing the cosmic energy that sustains the universe. His four arms represent the four cardinal directions and the various aspects of his power. The drum in his upper right hand symbolizes creation, the fire in his upper left hand signifies destruction, the fearlessness gesture of his lower right hand represents protection, and his raised lower left hand bestows blessings upon his devotees. Alignment with University Values: The dynamic energy and constant movement of the Nataraja dance resonate with the university's emphasis on innovation, creativity, and lifelong learning. The statue serves as a reminder to students to embrace challenges, overcome obstacles, and strive for continuous self-improvement. )
/E (Lord Shiva's Significance: Shiva, one of the principal deities in Hinduism, is revered as the supreme being, the source of all creation and destruction. His cosmic dance, embodied in the Nataraja form, signifies the cyclical nature of the universe, the constant interplay of creation and destruction, and the underlying rhythm of life itself. Symbolism of the Dance: The Nataraja statue portrays Shiva dancing within a ring of fire, representing the cosmic energy that sustains the universe. His four arms represent the four cardinal directions and the various aspects of his power. The drum in his upper right hand symbolizes creation, the fire in his upper left hand signifies destruction, the fearlessness gesture of his lower right hand represents protection, and his raised lower left hand bestows blessings upon his devotees. Alignment with University Values: The dynamic energy and constant movement of the Nataraja dance resonate with the university's emphasis on innovation, creativity, and lifelong learning. The statue serves as a reminder to students to embrace challenges, overcome obstacles, and strive for continuous self-improvement. )
