/T (Biographical Details of Lord Shiva: Unveiling the Mythological Figure  Lord Shiva, revered as one of the three supreme deities in Hinduism, alongside  Brahma and Vishnu, embodies a complex and fascinating figure. His  biographical details are interwoven with myths and legends, revealing his  multifaceted personality and immense power.  Shiva is often depicted as a powerful and fierce deity, associated with both  creation and destruction. He holds the power to both build and break down,  symbolizing the constant cycle of life and death. His immense energy is  represented by his blue skin, while his matted hair and third eye signify his  deep wisdom and connection to the divine.  One of the most iconic representations of Shiva is the Nataraja form, where he  dances within a ring of fire. This dance symbolizes the cyclical nature of the  universe, where creation and destruction are interconnected and necessary.  His four arms hold significant objects: )
