/T (The core message of the Nataraja lies in its depiction of Shiva's cosmic  dance. This dynamic movement symbolizes the cyclical nature of the  universe, where creation and destruction coexist in a constant interplay.  The fire that surrounds Shiva represents the destructive aspect,  signifying the impermanence of all things. Yet, amidst this fire, Shiva  dances with grace and serenity, reminding us that even within  destruction lies the potential for new beginnings. )
