/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The ring of fire surrounding Shiva also symbolizes Maya, the illusion of the material world. Maya seduces us with its transient pleasures and distracts us from the true reality. However, the Nataraja statue offers a glimpse beyond this illusion. Through Shiva's dance, we are reminded that the physical world is temporary and ever-changing. This message encourages us to delve deeper and seek a higher truth. It prompts us to question the nature of reality and explore the realm of the spiritual. By transcending the illusion of Maya, we can gain a deeper understanding of ourselves and our place in the universe. )
/E (The ring of fire surrounding Shiva also symbolizes Maya, the illusion of the material world. Maya seduces us with its transient pleasures and distracts us from the true reality. However, the Nataraja statue offers a glimpse beyond this illusion. Through Shiva's dance, we are reminded that the physical world is temporary and ever-changing. This message encourages us to delve deeper and seek a higher truth. It prompts us to question the nature of reality and explore the realm of the spiritual. By transcending the illusion of Maya, we can gain a deeper understanding of ourselves and our place in the universe. )
