/T (Death: The Nataraja statue also serves as a beacon of hope for spiritual seekers. By observing and understanding the cosmic dance, we can gain insight into the cycle of birth and death, known as Samsara. This cycle is driven by karma, the law of cause and effect. The statue offers a path to liberation from this cycle. By aligning ourselves with the divine energy represented by Shiva, we can break free from the shackles of karma and achieve Moksha, the ultimate liberation. This involves cultivating qualities like detachment, compassion, and self-realization. )
